xmodel/grok-vanrijn.log:1:I'll start by reading today's sweep, our promoted record, the HC4 adjudication, and van Rijn's repo so the verdict sits on the actual mathematics rather than the claim framing.There's already a van Rijn log in xmodel. Next I’ll pull our promoted record, the HC4 adjudication, and his public write-ups.I’ll pull paper1, the vertex-gap theorem, and race doctrine next, then clone van Rijn’s repo and read the write-ups.Cloning van Rijn’s repo off-workspace so I can read the write-ups without touching our tree.The full clone is large; I’ll fetch the key write-ups directly from GitHub while it finishes.Repo is cloned. Next I’ll read the (72,108), HC4, and (75,125) write-ups and grep for overlap with our record.The (72,108) write-ups match Helali’s lineage. I’ll read the HC4 and (75,125) programs next and check for tripwires against our unpublished work.Prop 4.3 checker passed. I have the overlap map; writing the adjudication now.**Collaboration, not threat.** Full write-up is in `xmodel/grok-vanrijn.md`.
