dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-eval-20260812.md:29:| 5 | **Mixed-merge children of residue-A (not of off-axis entries)** | BOOK-ENUM’s “\(M\ge 2\) chain engine” is about \(b_i\ge 2\) *entries*. The live hole is a *second* merge with all \(\mu_e\ge 2\) downstream of the \(M=2\) jump, legal at \(m\ge 3\). Either the book is missing cells, or the quarantine closes. | From child \(Q=(6,12,3,2,5)\), enumerate MP6(b)/(d) mixed merges with \(\mu_e\ge 2\), \(r\le 4\), \(\mathrm{td}\le 14\). Any new \((p,q)\) not among the 27 survivors cracks completeness. |
dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-eval-20260812.md:35:Dim-2 keeps proving the statements that are true (GMC(2), Shaska for every weight sign, no graded plane CE). Every known \(n\ge 3\) mechanism dies in the plane (Picard/\(d=3\) needle, no tangent-sweep, no graded escape). Eighty-five years without an example is evidence. Residue-A is the best formal candidate I have seen in this literature, but “passes the printed list” is exactly Theorem O, and an étale non-proper degree-6 endomorphism of \(\mathbb{A}^2\) is the thing JC2 says does not exist — consistency at vertices is cheap compared with algebraizing 126 series.
dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-eval-20260812.md:39:**Stall** where the program is already stalling: R1/depth-84/deferred-band descent on residue-A (artifacts, 1.5 TB deaths, discriminants receding). Next: TDU’s growing composite single-pole residual, which no finite book-bash can finish. DC(2) is the strongest *proof* route and is blocked on 2-dimensional Schur/Parshin; it will not be this campaign’s win.
dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-eval-20260812.md:41:The honest fork is unchanged since L1: residue-A is either a counterexample or it dies by mathematics that is not in Sigray. Printed-tier is exhausted (Theorem O). Treat the next kill attempt that is *not* a larger Groebner core as the real experiment.
