xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:3813:./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3051:SHEET6.md:21:- **The real wall is at 9, not 6**: Sigray exhibits a decorated Eggers–Wall tree satisfying ALL his constraints at td = 9 with (deg f, deg g) = (48,64) — Moh's exceptional case — matching Orevkov's holomorphic "counterexamples to JC at infinity" (minimal td 9, bidegree (48,64); DO-I: the local-at-infinity method can at best reach ~8). Sigray verbatim: the problem at higher degree is not that computations are "more involved" but that a consistent tree EXISTS at 9. Corollary: td ∈ {6,7,8} is the entire remaining runway for at-infinity methods, with no known consistency obstruction below 9.
