SHEET6.md-39-## 7. Verdict + pilot
SHEET6.md-40-- **Verdict: realistic weeks-scale multi-agent campaign — NOT a conceptual wall at 6.** The wall (consistent local datum) is proven only at td = 9/(48,64). Prerequisites in order: (a) foundations audit of Sigray §§2–8 [+ fetch Żołądek PDF for the reserve engine]; (b) mechanize + validate on td ≤ 5; (c) sweep td = 6. Even the failure mode (a surviving tree) produces a concrete bidegree target for the existing (72,108)-style exclusion pipeline. Prize: bound becomes td ≥ 7 — with 8-and-9 then the endgame of the whole at-infinity program (and 9 known unreachable locally ⇒ global methods required there regardless).
SHEET6.md-41-- **Pilot case (single best first task)**: mechanically re-derive **Prop 9.1's 11-row table and Statement 9.6** (propagation from Q(G) = (j,2j,3,2,5): Diophantine (k+2)ν/((k+1)ν+1) = (1+2n)/(5+n) with n ≡ 1 mod 3, expected output exactly {(21,15),(75,51),(20,16)} + λ-classification (i)–(v)) and diff against thesis pp. 45–53. Validates the enumerator on solved ground and forces the Q-propagation library into existence. First NEW case after the pilot: extend the table to Λ = 7 (pure Statement-5.2 arithmetic, bounded, agent-sized).
