xmodel/sol-avenues2.md-4-
xmodel/sol-avenues2.md-5-1. The best new lever is exact: Keller symplectic exactness forces the level-\(\kappa\) coefficient of every infinity series to vanish; at sheet 6 this gives nine level-42 pins, six of them immediately usable in the live residual system.
xmodel/sol-avenues2.md-6-2. The best direct attack on the nonlinear depth-21 survivor is to restore the toric relations discarded by the successful 5,106-column monomial relaxation; exact inconsistency would kill, while a reconstructible point would seed a disproof lift.
xmodel/sol-avenues2.md-7-3. The cheapest off-axis reducer is a proof-level classification of equality in every summand of Statement 9.4, aimed at the 1,390 exact-budget \(td=7\) routes; the sharp \((10,15)\) route is an important negative control.
xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:8:4. Two more global proof tests are worth pilots: Mittag-Leffler/adjoint compatibility of the Keller primitive and a genuinely gauge-free, depth-invariant coefficient holonomy—not another per-cell T1 solve.
xmodel/sol-avenues2.md-9-5. The explicit disproof lane is to positively lift a surviving exact-fit off-axis cell through successive Puiseux/Jacobian windows; the remaining multibranch-semigroup idea is cheaper but much more speculative.
